#
# SHA-256 digests of every executable and shared library that `cargo-anneal`
# loads from the toolchain directory, as `<arch>-<os>/<toolchain-relative path>`.
# A path ending in `/` locks the directory's top-level entry names (one per
# line, byte order) rather than file bytes; a path ending in `/**` locks the
# recursive content-tree digest of every regular file under that directory.
# (`Init.*` `.olean` modules are additionally locked by
# `trusted/lean/foundation-lock.json`.)
#
# FIXME(#87): Add aarch64-linux, x86_64-macos, and aarch64-macos lock entries
# once those platform toolchain archives are pinned.
#
# Lean 4.34.1: `lean` and the libraries its RUNPATH ($ORIGIN/../lib/lean)
# resolves. `lean/bin/lean` must also match foundation-lock.json.
